 result←object(State ∆Bitmap)arg;bmp;objname
 ⍝ Create and return a Bitmap "handle", which contains the pixel-contents of the bitmap
 ⍝ This handle should be "freed" later with '#' ∆WI '⎕Free'

 ⍝ '?Bitmap' bitmap ...

 result←⍬
 :If 1≥|≡arg ⋄ arg←,⊂arg ⋄ :EndIf
 '∆WI RANK ERROR: Bitmap'##.Error∨/2<≢¨⍴¨arg

 :For bmp :In arg
     :If ##.IsInt bmp ⍝ This better be a bitmap handle
     :AndIf 1=≢bmp
         result,←⊃bmp ⍝ Just return the same pointer intact
     :ElseIf (##.IsChar bmp)∧'>'∊bmp ⍝ This is a bitmap resource ⍝? Does this need more thorough validation?
         ##.Error'Bitmap resources are not supported yet' ⍝? Add this later
     :ElseIf ##.IsChar bmp ⍝ This is a bitmap file name
         '∆WI RANK ERROR: Bitmap'##.Error 1<≢⍴bmp←1/bmp
         :If '.bmp'≡⍥⎕C ¯4↑bmp ⍝ We're only accepting .BMP files ⍝? May do more later
         :AndIf ⎕NEXISTS bmp
             objname←(object⍕⍛,'.',##.Next object)##.∆WC'Bitmap'('File'bmp) ⍝ We'll create an object to use later
             ⍝ Build a "handle" namespace pointing to this bitmap for later reference
             result,←'Bitmap'CreateHandle(ObjName:objname ⋄ ∆EX:objname) ⍝ Just store the object-reference for later use
         :Else
             ##.Error'∆WI DRAW ERROR: Invalid or missing bitmap file "',bmp,'"'
         :EndIf
     :Else
         ##.Error'∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Bitmap'
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
